{"said": ["a cut apple browns because the knife breaks its cells and lets a caged enzyme, its fuel, and the air's oxygen finally meet \u2014 a build, not a rot; lemon juice slows it because the enzyme balks at acid.", "a sneeze seizes the room without permission, and bless-you is the room's ritual answer \u2014 interruption acknowledged, forgiven, and closed in one beat; the custom is far older than its favorite explanations (plague, escaping souls \u2014 UNSURE, likely backfilled).", "the room's air holds one level of dampness and every open food walks toward it from its own side \u2014 a chip is drier than the air, drinks, and goes limp; a cut loaf is wetter, exhales, and dries hard on top of its crystal-staling."], "ground": ""}